@startuml "Flyweight - Book - Class Diagram"
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title Flyweight — a book of shared characters


class Character <<ConcreteFlyweight>> {
  - value : char
  - upperCase : boolean
  + getValue() : char
}

class CharacterFactory <<FlyweightFactory>> {
  - characters : Map<String, Character>
  + createCharacter(c, upper) : Character
  + createdCount() : int
  + savedCount() : int
}

interface Factory
class Line {
  - chars : List<Character>
  - capacity : int
  + add(character) : boolean
  + characterAt(position) : Character
}
class Page
class Book

Factory <|.. CharacterFactory
CharacterFactory ..> Character : "pools by (value, case)"
Line o-- Character : "shared"
Page o-- Line
Book o-- Page

note right of Character
  <b>Two fields, both intrinsic.</b>
  Immutable, package-private
  constructor.

  It used to carry <b>line</b> and
  <b>position</b> as well — labelled
  extrinsic in a comment and
  stored anyway, which is what
  made it unshareable.
end note

note bottom of Line
  Position is the <b>index in this list</b>.
  It needed no home at all.

  236 characters -> <b>29</b> objects.
end note

note bottom of CharacterFactory
  The pool used to be a field
  that was <b>never read or written</b>,
  while createCharacter allocated
  on every call.
end note

@enduml
